<title>UK: Bulk carrier aground in Lake Superior.</title>
<headline>Bulk carrier aground in Lake Superior.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-09-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>The U.S.-registered bulk carrier George A. Stinson, 61,564 dwt, loaded with taconite, grounded late on Thursday in Whitefish Bay, Lake Superior, in lat 46 30 84n, long 84 37 16w., Lloyd's Shipping Intelligence Service said.</p>
<p>The vessel is still aground and refloating attempts are continuing. No injuries, damage or pollution were reported.</p>
